/S /P
/ActualText (1)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/T (PROVIDE SESSIONS TO 400 STUDENTS )
/E (PROVIDE SESSIONS TO 400 STUDENTS )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Visiting over 400 students ensures that we will reach a variety of schools, and interact with students from different demographics. A study by the University of Nevada, Reno emphasized the importance of collaborative hands-on activities as an important strategy to support a student in STEM \(Wiest, L. R. 2014\). Implementing that into our sessions, we brought a variety of activities, tailored to the needs and interests of students. For younger students, we taught basic lever systems through DIY candy catapults, and for older kids, we taught programming with basic loops, and they coded their LED vests \(see appendix for a full list of activities\).)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
305 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Additionally, we reached out to local organizations like STEM Like a Girl, Chick Tech, and Engaging Every Student to work on bringing STEM education to underserved communities. They were all very excited to join in our cause, and we hosted joint sessions with them to reach a wider audience. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
306 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [20]
>>
endobj
