495 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (When planning our session plan, we realized the most important aspect was our curriculum, and how we would differentiate it from a normal class environment. Unlike a traditional classroom where a teacher lectures for hours, we emphasized hands-on learning through interactive activities, which allowed for increased student concentration, retention of information, and interest in pursuing STEM. Additionally, we tailored our curriculum for different grade levels, what they were learning, and the number of students.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
